riven largely by a $51 million provision for financial systems modernization.\n*   **Title II (Security, Enforcement, & Investigations):** The largest component, receiving $40.00 billion. This title covers Customs and Border Protection (CBP), ICE, TSA, the Coast Guard, and the Secret Service. Funding increased by 4.1% over the request and 1.2% over FY2018.\n*   **Title III (Protection, Preparedness, Response, & Recovery):** Received $18.27 billion, a 42.3% increase over the request. This substantial rise was primarily due to the increased DRF allocation for FEMA.\n*   **Title IV (R&D, Training, & Services):** Received $1.62 billion, a modest 3.3% increase over the request, covering USCIS, FLETC, and the Science and Technology Directorate.\n*   **Title V (General Provisions):** Included $303 million in rescissions of prior-year funds and provisions directing $300 million of unobligated DRF balances to offset new appropriations.\n\nThe report also highlights the Department's transition to a Common Appropriations Structure (CAS) to improve transparency and standardize budgeting across components. Additionally, it provides technical context on budgetary concepts such as discretionary versus mandatory spending, offsetting collections, and the adjustments to discretionary spending caps under the Budget Control Act, specifically noting the historic use of the disaster relief cap adjustment in FY2019.", refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=None, audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=[], reasoning=None), stop_reason=None, token_ids=None)], created=1783841151, model='Qwen3.5-27B', object='chat.completion', service_tier=None, system_fingerprint=None, usage=CompletionUsage(completion_tokens=757, prompt_tokens=8426, total_tokens=9183, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), prompt_logprobs=None, prompt_token_ids=None, kv_transfer_params=None)

